1. searchParams
Suppose your URL is: /?category=shoes
{searchParams}: Destructures the incoming page properties to get the URL query parameters (the part after the ? in a URL).
searchParams contains { category: 'shoes'}  //It represents the query parameters from the URL.

searchParams: Promise<{ category: string }>
searchParamas returns a Promise -> it eventually returns an object.
Promise.resolve({
  category: "shoes"
})